{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs","id":1134762,"title":"Exigence grabs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-27T23:26:48-07:00","id":1134762,"title":"Exigence grabs","content":"We know exigence can be granted to various gods, and that it can be stolen, or ownership of a particular exigence transferred, once in circulation.<br /> <br /> So would demons and or the agents of the death lords make an effort to gain control of such things, or the gods who hold them? Would the Sidereals? Or maybe even some of the dragon blooded? Could the Yozi use stolen exigence to create new infernals, or something akin to them?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that the existence of the Exigence creates a whole new battlefield in creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 08-28-2017, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T23:39:43-07:00","id":1134764,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals already have their finger on the pulse of Exigence, from what the previous devs said - an office of the Bureau of Destiny is dedicated to tracking down Exigents, and the Sids have been doing their best to manipulate which gods receive the Exigence, and which mortals are granted it.<br /> <br /> Exigence, so we've been told, is limited to the gods. Which doesn't rule out someone <i>manipulating</i> a god...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T02:43:59-07:00","id":1134791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs#post1134762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that the existence of the Exigence creates a whole new battlefield in creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI've got to say, that's the kind of thing I specifically would not want it to be.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think there's a lot to the Exigence as it has been presented to us, a subject of intrigue distinct to Creation's gods. I think bringing in other entities of the setting dilutes that, distracts from ideas for minor or marginal gods who might get in on that black market, and would keep people from coming up with alternative origins for the possible Exalted of things like demons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T06:56:39-07:00","id":1134820,"title":"","content":"Exigence can only be used by gods. Demons, ghosts, and fae cannot use it or steal it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:09:12-07:00","id":1134891,"title":"","content":"Interesting... however that doesn't mean they can't interfere with the process, they can exert influence over the god in question, and it's not like things haven't messed with exaltations before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T15:29:01-07:00","id":1134971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs?p=1134891#post1134891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... and it's not like things haven't messed with exaltations before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is exactly why people don`t want it done again, to something we haven`t explored yet.<br /> <br /> Oh! Here is this great new thing, a way for lesser gods to get their Their Own Exalted Champions<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122! But NOPE! They just got jacked by demons, ghosts, w/e so they are just shitty Abyssals, Infernalss w/es...<br /> <br /> That is the drift, I guess.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:21:26-07:00","id":1135010,"title":"","content":"... annnnnd?<br /> <br /> I mean yeah it would be nice if the nice if the minor gods could make their own exalted without bigger badder guys breathing down their necks, but life ain't fair. There are plenty of people who if they found out about exigence would have reason to try to game the system, and a few of them could even go beyond merely influencing a god's choice of champions.<br /> <br /> The humans themselves would have a vested interest in how champions are chosen.<br /> <br /> That's not even getting into gods who may have thrown in with the sids, abyssals, or yozi.<br /> <br /> Or a Solar who decides to experiment.<br /> <br /> Exigence represents an incredibly useful resource, that makes it a potential battleground, even if gods are the only ones that can handle and bestow it.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't the various factions go after it in some form or another?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying every exigence is gonna get nabbed and played with, hell most of them probably happen in far off corners of creation that barely see Dragon born or lunars, to say nothing of the solaroids.<br /> <br /> But that said, I can't see the various factions ignoring it either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 08-28-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:52:06-07:00","id":1135015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs?p=1135010#post1135010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... annnnnd?<br /> <br /> I mean yeah it would be nice if the nice if the minor gods could make their own exalted without bigger badder guys breathing down their necks, but life ain't fair. There are plenty of people who if they found out about exigence would have reason to try to game the system, and a few of them could even go beyond merely influencing a god's choice of champions.<br /> <br /> The humans themselves would have a vested interest in how champions are chosen.<br /> <br /> That's not even getting into gods who may have thrown in with the sids, abyssals, or yozi.<br /> <br /> Or a Solar who decides to experiment.<br /> <br /> Exigence represents an incredibly useful resource, that makes it a potential battleground, even if gods are the only ones that can handle and bestow it.<br /> <br /> Why wouldn't the various factions go after it in some form or another?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying every exigence is gonna get nabbed and played with, hell most of them probably happen in far off corners of creation that barely see Dragon born or lunars, to say nothing of the solaroids.<br /> <br /> But that said, I can't see the various factions ignoring it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's been said, definitively, that <i>only the gods can use the Exigence</i>. Furthermore, access to the Exigence is granted personally by the Unconquered Sun in response to a god's petition.<br /> <br /> Now, we know that messing around with it is possible:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As some people have begun to speculate, the Black Market Exaltations refer to Exigents made illicitly, somehow bypassing the Unconquered Sun's erm firewall, so to speak.<br /> <br /> In the most literal terms, there were raw Exaltations granted by the Unconquered Sun which were then not used by the petitioner, but instead passed into the world of spirits, where it cycled the realms of gods and men until a bidder was finally able to trigger it.<br /> <br /> A &quot;dirty bomb&quot; (not actual game term) Exaltation is a similar concept, only the Exaltation has passed through the hands of multiple spirits who have modified the power inside. This only happens for nefarious, terrible reasons, as the resulting Exigent is always an aberration of enormous power.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the fact that <i>some</i> tampering with the process of Exigent creation is possible does not mean <i>anything </i>is. Solars can't use the Exigence. Demons can't. Fair folk can't. Even elementals, who are theoretically part of the Bureaucracy, can't. <br /> <br /> Like, yes, Yu-Shan is very political and undoubtedly there are power-plays being made whereby a god convinces a weaker god to try to gain access to the Exigence and create an Exalt for purposes that are ultimately the stronger god's (replace &quot;stronger god&quot; with &quot;Sidereals,&quot; even), but that's <i>very different</i> from &quot;we should just open up Exigents to be Exalts of whatever, because anybody could have messed with the Exaltation.&quot; This is missing the Doylist point that Abyssals and Infernals exist to be commentary on Solars and foil them in interesting ways, which is why their Exaltations are capable of being mucked with at the Watsonian level. What would be the point of foils to a splat that has the unifying feature of incredible diversity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T21:43:43-07:00","id":1135059,"title":"","content":"Headdesk<br /> <br /> That is what you make me want to do.<br /> <br /> Even if gods are the only ones with admin privileges doesn't preclude the other factions from interfering. <br /> <br /> Gods are easy to influence, especially if they're not gods associated with integrity or social skills.<br /> <br /> A demon could give a god something to include as part of an exigence, or even just a special artifact to go with it. A human or an elemental could convince them to do something off base via regular old social skills and bribery. An actual abyssal or infernal could easily browbeat them into compliance, or offer them aid and support in getting the exigence in exchange for some say in who gets it, or just to get into position to be a mentor figure to the new exalt and gain their support that way.<br /> <br /> They'd never even need to see the damned exigence to exert influence over when it's used and upon whom. <br /> <br /> I never said off-brand solaroids, that was where someone else went, although it's certainly a possibility if gods can add things to the exigence then they can probably add something someone gave them, however a river god + a little something something from a demon isn't going to make an exalted of Kimberry, it's going to make an exalted of that river god with a little malfean flavor, and possibly add a few intimacies for certain players in the brass city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T21:45:18-07:00","id":1135060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs?p=1135010#post1135010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't the various factions go after it in some form or another?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of the Exigence is to showcase how Exaltation expresses itself in many different miraculous forms and reducing other Exaltations to the Exigence instead of creating new Exaltations completely defeats the purpose of having the Exigence in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T22:26:12-07:00","id":1135071,"title":"","content":"Huh? I'm not even sure what you're accusing me of at this point. Whose exaltations am I reducing to the exigence? What does that even mean? If creating new exalts was easy everyone would do it, the exigence is a source of new exaltations and is thus a valuable resource.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T04:22:26-07:00","id":1135122,"title":"","content":"Nobody is accusing you of anything, you're just defensive of an idea the majority of those that cared to respond aren't fond of.<br /> <br /> People are tired of everything having a finger in every pie and want somethings to be their own isolated thing too.<br /> <br /> So knock yourself out with your homebrew Yozigence. But don't be upset people are not as excited about it as you are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T05:23:06-07:00","id":1135131,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11837\" data-vbnamecard=\"11837\">A Not Quite Simple Soul</a>: I went back and reread your posts in this thread, and as far as I can tell, you have two positions:<br /> <br /> A: &quot;Exigents are a potent tool, and powerful entities might attempt to suborn lesser gods, or wait and suborn the Exigents themselves after Exaltation, in order to use them for their own purposes.&quot; I don't think anyone disagrees with this. This sort of thing is true throughout the setting. Heck, out in Skullstone there is a <i>Solar</i> working loyally for a <i>Deathlord</i>. Everyone wants them some Exalted servants.<br /> <br /> B: &quot;Exigents are a potent tool, and there exist other messed-with Exaltations in the game, so powerful entities might mess with a granted Exigence, so we might see something like the Yozis using stolen Exigence.&quot; This is what people are jumping on and don't want to see, because the freeform nature of Exigents means that this can thematically crowd out all of those entities' own champions. That's what Tiresias meant about reducing other Exalts to the Exigence: the metanarrative reason Exigents are restricted to gods is so that Exigents can reflect the themes of the thousands of little gods in Creation and open the door to having them and their portfolios matter to the game and setting, and if Deathlords or demons or whoever metaphysically mess with the Exigence itself, it shoves the little gods out of the spotlight designed for them and <i>also</i> makes the eventual Exalted servants of whoever messed with it (Abyssals, Infernals, etc.) less special and unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T08:54:26-07:00","id":1135169,"title":"","content":"I feel kind of bad about my initial response.<br /> <br /> \u200bFirst off, when it comes to Exigents, excessive focus on arguments reliant on diegesis, the statement of &quot;this made up thing wouldn't work that way because it violates the made up rules&quot;, is really just heading down a logical cul-de-sac. And to whatever extent that those rules were devised for the sake of a real world implication (per my speculation, to encourage storytelling more strongly focused on the gods), it's an implication with fairly low stakes.<br /> <br /> \u200bBefore I can try to comment on any other developing ideas, I have a question for A Not Quite Simple Soul; whether the query is about how a thing might work within the logic of the setting, or if it's about stories that you already have in mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:09:40-07:00","id":1135265,"title":"","content":"Well initially I was just wondering if there were obvious people to be involved in this, I mean the yozi are a vast multitude, who or what among their numbers would be ideal for exigence influencing and god herding? Would it be a project for the big names or would the lesser Yozi pounce on this as an opportunity to get their own exalted servitors and assets? Do the lunars out in the weeds plotting the end of the scarlet empire and the immaculate faith even know what exigence is? Would the gold and/or bronze factions make a concerted effort to contact exigents? Would DBs make an effort to organize the process within their domains or are they too invested in their one true exalt narrative?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1134762-exigence-grabs?p=1135131#post1135131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11837\" data-vbnamecard=\"11837\">A Not Quite Simple Soul</a>:<br /> B: &quot;Exigents are a potent tool, and there exist other messed-with Exaltations in the game, so powerful entities might mess with a granted Exigence, so we might see something like the Yozis using stolen Exigence.&quot; This is what people are jumping on and don't want to see, because the freeform nature of Exigents means that this can thematically crowd out all of those entities' own champions. That's what Tiresias meant about reducing other Exalts to the Exigence: the metanarrative reason Exigents are restricted to gods is so that Exigents can reflect the themes of the thousands of little gods in Creation and open the door to having them and their portfolios matter to the game and setting, and if Deathlords or demons or whoever metaphysically mess with the Exigence itself, it shoves the little gods out of the spotlight designed for them and <i>also</i> makes the eventual Exalted servants of whoever messed with it (Abyssals, Infernals, etc.) less special and unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an actual concern yes, which is why I asked about the possibility, if I understand the timeline correctly then the exigence was created before the abyssals and internals strode into town, so it may not be protected from whatever dickery the yozi and deathlords/neverborn unloaded on their captured exaltations.<br /> <br /> However I'm not proposing the they'd be able to set up factories for for their exalt types.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is that the exigence is meant to be handled by gods, i'd expect that it requires input from a god in order to function. So even an abyss tainted exigence would be primarily built on the basis of the god's themes, just warped and twisted. So maybe if the exaltation would normally allow them to reach celestial sorcery it instead allows them to become 2nd circle necromancers, maybe it makes them attune to soul steel. Maybe a local elemental would be willing to give a god some of it's power in order to help it exalt a champion to defend their home and it causes the resulting exalt to blend that elemental's elements into it's primary patron's themes.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of ways for the big guys to dick with the exaltations without overriding the little guys themes, really subtlety may well be a virtue in such machinations. Maybe they wouldn't' even touch the exaltation itself just slide the patron an artifact that would allow them to exert influence upon the exalt during it's development phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}